# NOTHING IN HERE GOES TO GIT.
#
# This directory holds signing material: a private key, a certificate signing
# request, and a provisioning profile. The repository is PUBLIC (CLAUDE.md rule
# 6), and a leaked signing key is worse than a leaked secret — it is not a
# credential to something, it is the identity ITSELF. Anyone holding it can sign
# software as this developer, and the only remedy is revoking the certificate
# and invalidating every build ever signed with it.
#
# Ignored wholesale rather than by extension: the next file added here will be
# sensitive too, and an allowlist is the wrong default for a folder like this.
*
!.gitignore
